-# Deck controls — beta 2 freeze mitigation
+# Deck beta 3 - host character-selection freeze candidate
+
+Beta 3 removes the native base calls from CustomButton.StartHover and StopHover.
+IL2CPP generated virtual wrappers can redispatch into these injected overrides,
+causing recursive calls. Managed hover callbacks remain. The menu displays
+Deck beta 3; protocol and assembly version remain 5.1.0. No other gameplay or
+networking code changed. Native base hover visuals are not restored here.
+
+The reported host freeze stops animation during character selection. This
+candidate removes a matching code-level suspect; the freeze has not been
+reproduced or confirmed fixed on a Steam Deck. The known connection-timeout,
+menu-state and networking-reset bugs remain outside this narrow candidate.
+
+Windows verification: Release PROTON build passed, 12 compiled-DLL DeckSmoke
+checks passed, and 8 compiled-IL/dependency checks passed. The IL regression
+rejects the shipped beta 2 DLL's two native base hover calls. Resolved packages
+and dependency assembly identities match beta 2. No Unity or Deck runtime test
+was performed. Before calling this fixed, host a room, move focus onto and away
+from Show Room Code, select a character, continue to map selection, and start
+with a second player. Preserve BepInEx/LogOutput.log from a failing run.
+
+The following documents the cumulative beta 2 features and build procedure.
 
